From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 011/191] [ae-patch] Add a Run button to chat shell code blocks
 that pastes into the session's shell

A session on a host with shells often replies with a command block, which
today is copied by hand into a shell, often on a phone. Assistant code blocks
tagged bash, sh, shell, zsh, console or powershell, or untagged blocks that
read as commands, get a Run button beside the wrap and copy buttons, for the
owner of a session whose agent declares shells (the "+ New shell" gate).

Run opens a confirm sheet with the exact text, a plain warning for sudo,
rm -rf, curl | sh and dd, and a hint when a heredoc, a quote or a line
continuation is still open, in which case the block is pasted without Enter.
On Run the session's selected or newest live shell (or a new default shell,
through the existing create route) opens as a rail tab, or full screen on a
phone, and the text is written with xterm's own paste followed by an Enter
keystroke: the same onData path and WebSocket the keyboard uses. No server
endpoint is added and sudo still asks for the password in the terminal.

Logic lives in new files (lib/aeRunCommand.ts, lib/aeTerminalInput.ts,
shell/useAeRunInTerminal.ts, components/AeRunCodeButton.tsx). Upstream files
change by a few lines each: two methods on TerminalSession, a registration in
TerminalView for writable attaches, the button in ChatCodeBlockPre, and the
hook call in AppShell.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
